{"name":"Treasure Isle","hex":"#609d91","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"treasure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A collection of valuable things; accumulated wealth; a stock of money, jewels, etc.","Anything greatly valued."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consider to be precious; to value highly.","To store or stow in a safe place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasure"},{"term":"isle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An island, usually very small. Compare with islet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Obsolete spelling of aisle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Treasure Isle (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Treasure Isle is a defunct browser-based video game by Zynga for Facebook, launched in April 2010. It allowed users to dig for treasure on various islands. The game was discontinued on December 5, 2012."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasure_Isle_(video_game)"},{"title":"Treasure","blocks":[{"text":"Treasure is a concentration of wealth — often originating from ancient history — that is considered lost and/or forgotten until rediscovered. Some jurisdictions legally define what constitutes treasure, such as in the British Treasure Act 1996."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasure"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Treasure of Villena, one of the most important prehistoric golden tabl